  "document_title": "IEEE Std 802.15.4 LR-WPAN + Zigbee Specification",
  "version": "IEEE 802.15.4 (2.4 GHz O-QPSK PHY) + Zigbee Pro / Zigbee 3.0",
  "revised_date": "2024",
  "manufacturer": "IEEE 802.15 Working Group; Connectivity Standards Alliance (CSA)",
  "copyright": "© IEEE (802.15.4) and © Connectivity Standards Alliance (Zigbee)",
  "abstract": "A low-rate wireless personal area network (LR-WPAN) SoC built on IEEE Std 802.15.4 for the Physical and MAC layers and the Zigbee specification for the Network (NWK), Application Support (APS), Zigbee Device Object (ZDO) and Zigbee Cluster Library (ZCL) layers. The 2.4 GHz PHY uses Offset-QPSK (O-QPSK) with half-sine pulse shaping over Direct Sequence Spread Spectrum (DSSS, 32 chips/symbol, 2.0 Mchip/s) across 16 channels (channel 11-26), giving 250 kbps. The MAC provides CSMA-CA channel access, a beacon-enabled superframe with Guaranteed Time Slots (GTS), 16-bit PAN IDs, and 16-bit short plus 64-bit extended (EUI-64) addresses, with Full-Function (FFD) and Reduced-Function (RFD) devices. Zigbee adds star/tree/mesh networking (Coordinator / Router / End Device roles), endpoint/cluster-based applications, and AES-128 CCM* security with a network key, link keys and a Trust Center.",
  "keywords": [
    "IEEE 802.15.4",
    "Zigbee",
    "LR-WPAN",
